@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+---
+id: dl-005-cancellation-full-refund-before-the-rental-starts-none-after-cancelled-bookings-free-their-item
+type: decision-log
+title: "Cancellation: full refund before the rental starts, none after; cancelled bookings free their item"
+status: pending
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+## Context
+
+The request gave no refund rule, only that the customer gets an amount back, that a cancelled booking no
+longer holds its equipment and that a booking can be cancelled once.
+
+## Decision
+
+Cancelled before the rental starts (`at` strictly before `start`): the whole total is refunded. At or
+after the start: nothing is refunded. `at` is any UTC ISO-8601 instant, not only a whole hour. A
+cancelled booking is removed from the held bookings, so its item is free again; cancelling it a second
+time, like an unknown id, throws. An invalid `at` throws and leaves the booking in place.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The refund rule is an assumption of the developer and is the part to confirm with the school (for
+instance a partial refund close to the start); it lives in one line of `cancel`. Bookings are kept in a
+map by id.
